# Frontend environment — development only.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` if you need it. Most people will not: the default is correct when Spring
# Boot is running on localhost:8080, which is what `mvn spring-boot:run` and the Docker Compose
# file both give you.
#
# There is one variable, and it is read by vite.config.js at dev-server start — never by anything
# under src/. The application talks to its API with relative URLs (`/api/products`), proxied by the
# Vite dev server in development and by nginx in production, so there is no API base URL that can
# be wrong in one environment and right in the other. That is the whole reason this file is almost
# empty, and it is worth keeping it that way.

# Where the dev server should forward /api and /actuator.
# Change this if the backend is on another port, in a container with a published port, or on another
# machine on your network.
VITE_API_TARGET=http://localhost:8080
